# Documentation (`docs/`)

| File | Role |
| ---- | ---- |
| [technical-task.md](../../docs/technical-task.md) | product, entities, screens, API, limits, scenarios |
| [architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md) | layers, repo layout, flows, scaling |
| [tech-stack.md](../../docs/tech-stack.md) | fixed stack (do not propose alternatives unless asked) |
| [DESIGN.md](../../docs/DESIGN.md) | visual system and UI tokens |
| [frontend-implementation-plan.md](../../docs/frontend-implementation-plan.md) | step-by-step frontend delivery plan |

## Edit rules

- Write docs **in Russian**, concise, use tables where useful.
- Treat stack and v1 boundaries as **fixed**; disputed swaps (Redis, S3, Docker PG) only as “later / option A” in [architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md) §5, not as the current choice.
- When changing limits, TTL, formats, or auth — sync [task](../../docs/technical-task.md) ↔ [architecture](../../docs/architecture.md) ↔ [tech-stack](../../docs/tech-stack.md).
- Do not duplicate long sections across files; link, e.g. `[tech-stack.md](./tech-stack.md)`.
- Do not describe out-of-scope v1 features as already accepted ([architecture](../../docs/architecture.md) §6).
